    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `locality` field on owner creation. When an owner is created, their response now includes `locality`: `\"local\"` if their city is the single most common city among existing owners at that moment, otherwise `\"remote\"`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (matching sibling `Assign*` steps), I made four changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient String locality` field with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` and lets MapStruct's by-name mapping carry it into the response automatically.\n\n3. **`AssignLocality.java`** (new) \u2014 counts existing owners per city (the new owner isn't persisted yet, so it isn't counted), finds the max, and sets `\"local\"` only when exactly one city holds that max and it equals the new owner's city; otherwise `\"remote\"`. A tie for most-common yields `\"remote\"` (no *single* most common city), as does an empty owner set or a null city. Runs after `NormalizeCity`, so cities compare on their canonical spelling \u2014 consistent with `AssignCustomerCode`/`AssignSharesHousehold`.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignLocality` step (under the `transaction` governance) between `assignSharesHousehold` and `save`.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp18Tests` (local-when-most-common / remote-otherwise) passes, along with the whole suite.",
